      "body": "<!-- markdownlint-disable -->\n\n## Overview\n\nFollow-up to #64282. vLLM main refuses `--use-replayssm` for Nemotron-3.5-Transcribe, and every serve command in\nthe model card passes it. This PR declares ReplaySSM support for the model.\n\n## Claims\n\n- vLLM accepts `--use-replayssm` for `Nemotron3_5TranscribeForConditionalGeneration`. NemotronH already sizes the\n  ReplaySSM buffers; the wrapper only declares `SupportsReplaySSM`.\n- On Model Runner V2, every configuration in the card starts and serves with ReplaySSM (table below).\n- CI now runs the model's tests that need the published checkpoint.\n\n## Validation\n\nOn main before this PR, the card's serve command stops at startup: `ValueError: --use-replayssm is not supported for\narchitecture 'Nemotron3_5TranscribeForConditionalGeneration'`.\n\nWith this PR, on an RTX PRO 6000 (Blackwell) with the BF16 checkpoint and Model Runner V2, every configuration\nstarts, and 24 short clips get the same transcript from chat completions and from `/v1/audio/transcriptions`:\n\n| Configuration | Endpoints agree | Mean acceptance length |\n|---|---|---|\n| MTP8 (the card's default) | 24/24 | 7.25 |\n| MTP2 | 24/24 | 3.00 |\n| No speculative decoding | 24/24 | – |\n| DFlash2 K=7 | 24/24 | 5.46 |\n\nFrom `tests/`, with Hub access, all pass: `models/test_registry.py -k Nemotron3_5Transcribe` (2),\n`models/multimodal/processing/test_nemotron3_5_transcribe.py` (30),\n`models/multimodal/processing/test_common.py -k Nemotron-3.5-Transcribe` (3),\n`models/test_initialization.py -k Nemotron3_5Transcribe` (2),\n`models/multimodal/processing/test_tensor_schema.py -k Nemotron-3.5-Transcribe` (1).\n\n<details>\n<summary>Serve command</summary>\n\n```bash\nvllm serve nvidia/NVIDIA-Nemotron-3.5-Transcribe-30B-A4B --dtype bfloat16 --gpu-memory-utilization 0.94 \\\n  --max-model-len 65536 --max-num-batched-tokens 4096 --max-num-seqs 192 \\\n  --enable-chunked-prefill --no-enable-prefix-caching \\\n  --use-replayssm --mamba-backend flashinfer --mamba-cache-mode none \\\n  --mm-processor-cache-gb 0 --no-async-scheduling \\\n  --limit-mm-per-prompt '{\"audio\":{\"count\":6,\"length\":120000000}}' \\\n  --reasoning-parser nemotron_v3 \\\n  --default-chat-template-kwargs '{\"enable_thinking\": false}' \\\n  --speculative-config '{\"method\":\"mtp\",\"num_speculative_tokens\":8}'\n```\n\nMTP2 sets `\"num_speculative_tokens\":2`, no speculative decoding drops `--speculative-config`, and DFlash2 uses\n`'{\"method\":\"dflash\",\"num_speculative_tokens\":7,\"model\":\"nvidia/NVIDIA-Nemotron-3.5-Transcribe-30B-A4B-DFlash2\"}'`.\n</details>\n\n## Details\n\n- **Root cause.** `VllmConfig` refuses `--use-replayssm` unless the architecture declares `SupportsReplaySSM`.\n  NemotronH declares it, but the Transcribe wrapper contains a NemotronH decoder rather than subclassing it, so the\n  flag was missing. The wrapper already passes the Mamba state shape, dtype and copy-function calls to NemotronH,\n  which adds the ReplaySSM ring buffers, so the declaration is the whole fix.\n- **Constraints.** With speculative decoding, vLLM's FlashInfer ReplaySSM needs `--mamba-backend flashinfer` and\n  `--no-enable-prefix-caching`; the card sets both, and the docs note now says so.\n- **Model Runner V1.** The card currently selects V1 for the NeMo vLLM plugin's word timestamps. Since Model Runner\n  V1 is being removed, this PR is validated on V2 only.\n- **CI coverage.** CI cannot serve the 30B checkpoint end to end, so the serving validation above ran locally. With\n  the registry entries online, CI runs the model's registry, initialization, processing and tensor-schema tests.\n- **Related PRs.** No open PR changes these lines. #65379 (native CTC word timestamps) also edits the model file.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n\nAI assistance (Cursor agent) was used to prepare this change. Dongji Gao reviewed every changed line and the\nvalidation.\n",
